 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "The wind is born again.\nA carpet of white snows, like flowers,\nWhispers in the nightingales' hollow\nLike a fond mistress's hand\nOf dying pearls.  The winter\nIs not waning nor growing colder,\nBut as one comes to know it better\nShe carries its moody beauty\nAnd makes her heart tingle with\nIts coldness and sweetness.\nIt is come; and only from afar\nStill on whose lips frozen flowers",
